From: Arun Babu Neelicattu <arun.neelicattu@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Fix CLI HTTPS support when built with USE_SYSTEM_HTTPLIB

When USE_SYSTEM_HTTPLIB is enabled, pkg_search_module might not locate
a .pc file for cpp-httplib (e.g. on Fedora where cpp-httplib-devel ships
CMake config files instead). This leaves HTTPLIB_VERSION unset, causing
HTTPLIB_SUPPORTS_MBEDTLS to evaluate to FALSE.

As a result, CPPHTTPLIB_MBEDTLS_SUPPORT is omitted from target compile
definitions for the lemonade CLI target, leading to runtime error:
"Error listing models: HTTPS support is not compiled in this client."

Enable HTTPLIB_SUPPORTS_MBEDTLS whenever USE_SYSTEM_HTTPLIB is set, as
the distro mbedtls development package is linked.

---
 src/cpp/cli/CMakeLists.txt | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cpp/cli/CMakeLists.txt b/src/cpp/cli/CMakeLists.txt
index d28c308..75dfa3b 100640
--- a/src/cpp/cli/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/cpp/cli/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -192,6 +192,8 @@ if(NOT USE_SYSTEM_HTTPLIB)
     set(HTTPLIB_SUPPORTS_MBEDTLS TRUE)
 elseif(HTTPLIB_VERSION AND NOT HTTPLIB_VERSION VERSION_LESS "0.31.0")
     set(HTTPLIB_SUPPORTS_MBEDTLS TRUE)
+elseif(USE_SYSTEM_HTTPLIB)
+    set(HTTPLIB_SUPPORTS_MBEDTLS TRUE)
 endif()
 
 if(HTTPLIB_SUPPORTS_MBEDTLS)
-- 
